from __future__ import annotations

NAME = "Titan, the Veiled Moon"
AMBIENCE = "Gentle Rain"

# A soothing sleep-lecture about Saturn's great moon under a golden haze, with rivers and seas of liquid methane.
SECTIONS = [['You are lying down now, and there is nothing left to do.', 'Let your body grow heavy against whatever holds you.', 'There is no hurry here, and nowhere else you need to be.', 'Let your shoulders soften and sink a little lower.', 'Feel the weight of your hands resting wherever they have come to rest.', 'Let your breathing slow, easy and unforced.', 'Breathe in softly, and let the breath go even more softly.', 'With each breath out, let a little more of the day fall away.', 'Imagine a warmth, golden and dim, gathering gently around you.', 'You are beginning to float now, drifting up and away from the room.', 'Far ahead of you, wrapped in soft golden haze, a quiet moon is waiting.', 'Let yourself drift slowly toward it as you breathe.'], ['Far out past the warm light of the sun, a great ringed planet turns slowly in the dark.', 'Around that planet circles a moon called Titan, and you are drifting gently toward it.', 'Titan is the largest of all the moons that travel around Saturn.', 'It is so large that it is the second biggest moon in the whole solar system.', 'It is even a little larger than the small planet Mercury, though it is only a moon.', 'From far away it does not look sharp or bright, but soft and veiled.', 'A haze wraps it completely, so you cannot see its surface from space.', 'The whole world glows a gentle orange, like a lamp left low through the night.', 'Long ago, in the year sixteen fifty five, a quiet astronomer named Christiaan Huygens first saw it.', 'He looked through an early telescope and noticed this small light beside Saturn.', 'For centuries after, it remained a soft mystery, a golden dot in the dark.', 'And now you are floating closer to it, slow and unafraid.'], ['As you drift nearer, Titan grows from a dot into a great glowing sphere.', 'Almost every moon you might imagine is bare rock and empty silence.', 'But Titan is different, for Titan is wrapped in a real atmosphere.', 'It is the only moon in the whole solar system with a thick, substantial sky.', 'Its air is made mostly of nitrogen, the same gas that fills most of the air you are breathing now.', 'High in that air, a soft haze tints everything a warm and dreamy gold.', 'The atmosphere is so deep that at the surface it presses thicker than the air on Earth.', 'If you could stand there, the sky would not be blue but a hazy amber glow.', 'The light that reaches the ground is dim and golden, like the last hour before dusk.', 'Layers of orange haze drift high above, soft and slow and endless.', 'There is no harsh sun here, only a gentle, filtered light.', 'Let that warm amber light settle over you as you breathe out slowly.'], ['This is a cold and quiet world, far from the warmth of the sun.', 'On Titan the cold is deep, around a hundred and seventy nine degrees below zero.', 'It is so cold that water there is hard as stone, frozen into ice.', 'And yet, wonderfully, Titan is not a dry world at all.', 'It is the only place besides Earth with stable liquid resting on its surface.', 'But the liquid here is not water, for water cannot flow in such cold.', 'Instead, the rivers and lakes of Titan are made of liquid methane and ethane.', 'What would be a gas on Earth becomes a gentle liquid in this deep chill.', 'There are rivers that wind through the hills, carved slowly over long ages.', 'There is rain that falls from the hazy golden clouds.', 'And near the poles, there are great lakes and seas lying calm and still.', 'Imagine those quiet pools, dark and smooth, mirroring the amber sky above.'], ['Near the cold poles of Titan lie seas large enough to have names.', 'One is called Kraken Mare, a vast sea of liquid methane, the largest of them all.', 'Another is called Ligeia Mare, smooth and dark and deeply still.', 'These seas are wider than many of the great lakes upon the Earth.', 'Their surfaces are so calm that they barely ripple at all.', 'Picture standing at the shore of such a sea under a soft golden haze.', 'The methane is clear and cold, lapping slowly against a quiet beach.', 'Now and then a gentle rain falls upon the sea from the clouds above.', 'The drops are large and fat, and they fall slowly in the low gravity.', 'Each drop drifts down softly, taking its time to reach the ground.', 'It is a slow and patient rain, never harsh, never hurried.', 'Let those slow falling drops carry your thoughts gently downward too.'], ['Long after Huygens first saw this moon, we sent a spacecraft to visit it.', 'A craft called Cassini traveled for years across the dark to reach Saturn.', 'Cassini circled the ringed planet and mapped the veiled face of Titan again and again.', 'It peered through the haze with patient eyes and traced the rivers and the seas.', 'And Cassini carried a small companion, a probe named Huygens after the astronomer.', 'In the year two thousand and five, that little probe was released toward the moon.', 'It opened a parachute and drifted down slowly through the thick golden haze.', 'Down and down it floated, gentle and unhurried, into the orange sky.', 'At last it touched the surface, the most distant landing humans have ever made.', 'It came to rest softly on a plain scattered with small rounded pebbles.', 'Those pebbles were smooth and rounded, shaped over ages by flowing liquid.', 'On this far moon, as on a riverbed at home, the liquid had rounded the stones.'], ['Now let yourself drift down toward Titan, the way the little probe once did.', 'You are floating gently through the high golden haze, slow and weightless.', 'The amber light wraps around you, soft and dim and warm.', 'Down through the orange clouds you sink, with nothing to hurry you.', 'A slow methane rain falls beside you, the big drops drifting lazily down.', 'You fall as gently as they do, easy and calm and unafraid.', 'Below you the quiet sea lies dark and smooth and still.', 'Closer and closer you drift, until you settle softly on the gentle shore.', 'The smooth rounded pebbles are warm beneath you, and you sink into rest.', 'The golden haze closes softly over you like a blanket of warm light.', 'Let yourself grow heavier, sinking down, deeper and deeper into stillness.', 'Rest now on that far quiet moon, and drift gently down into sleep.']]
